# CodeQL Query Suite - Python Exclusions
# Filters out false positives where custom sanitization is verified but not
# automatically recognized by CodeQL's dataflow analysis.
#
# Related: Issue #MVA-2605

- description: Exclude py/full-ssrf in external_importer.py (validated via _validate_git_url)
- query: py/full-ssrf
- exclude:
    file:
      - autobot-backend/skills/external_importer.py

# #14126: the three call sites CodeQL flags in api/secrets.py log
# `secret_log_ref(id)` — a truncated SHA-256 of the identifier, not the
# identifier and never the secret value. The taint tracker follows the id into
# the helper and does not recognise the hash as a sanitiser, so it reports what
# is already the fix for what it is reporting: before this, one of those lines
# logged the id in full.
#
# Inline `codeql[...]` comments do not dismiss alerts here (#12307), so this is
# the only mechanism available. The scope is wider than the finding — it covers
# the whole file, including any genuine clear-text logging added later — which
# is tracked as its own trade-off rather than accepted silently.
- description: Exclude py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data in api/secrets.py (ids are logged as truncated SHA-256 via secret_log_ref)
- query: py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data
- exclude:
    file:
      - autobot-backend/api/secrets.py
